  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '- 8x8 board, all squares used, 16 pieces each; the back row starts empty.

    -
    Orthogonal movement only - no diagonals.

    - Men move forward, left, or right;
    they capture in all four directions.

    - No 180-degree turn: you can''t reverse
    straight back through the square you just left.

    - Capturing is mandatory
    - you must play the path that captures the most pieces.

    - Captured pieces
    are removed immediately - this can open new paths mid-turn.

    - The Dama (king)
    slides and captures any distance in a straight line.

    - A piece only crowns
    if it finishes its turn on the back row.

    - White always moves first.

    -
    Win by capturing every piece, blocking every legal move, or reducing your opponent
    to one man against your Dama.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1ab011c2eea9af9458b3d8873278ece5, type: 2}
